        ":question/id": "0d65088b-5dd5-54dd-9a0b-5bf7809d3991",
        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
        ":question/problem": "If $f(x)=\\frac{x^{2} + 2 \\sin{\\left(x \\right)}}{e^{x} + 3 \\cos{\\left(x \\right)}}$, find $f^{\\prime}(x)$ wherever the original quotient is defined.",
        ":question/worked-solution": "In this case, the expression for $f(x)$ is a quotient $\\frac{u(x)}{v(x)}$ with $u(x)=x^{2} + 2 \\sin{\\left(x \\right)}$ and $v(x)=e^{x} + 3 \\cos{\\left(x \\right)}.$\n\nTherefore, we apply the quotient rule as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f^{\\prime}(x)&=\\frac{u^{\\prime}(x)\\cdot v(x)-u(x)\\cdot v^{\\prime}(x)}{[v(x)]^{2}}\\\\ &=\\frac{(x^{2} + 2 \\sin{\\left(x \\right)})^{\\prime}\\cdot (e^{x} + 3 \\cos{\\left(x \\right)})-(x^{2} + 2 \\sin{\\left(x \\right)})\\cdot (e^{x} + 3 \\cos{\\left(x \\right)})^{\\prime}}{(e^{x} + 3 \\cos{\\left(x \\right)})^{2}}\\\\ &=\\frac{(2 x + 2 \\cos{\\left(x \\right)})\\cdot (e^{x} + 3 \\cos{\\left(x \\right)})-(x^{2} + 2 \\sin{\\left(x \\right)})\\cdot (e^{x} - 3 \\sin{\\left(x \\right)})}{(e^{x} + 3 \\cos{\\left(x \\right)})^{2}}\\\\ &=\\frac{- x^{2} e^{x} + 3 x^{2} \\sin{\\left(x \\right)} + 2 x e^{x} + 6 x \\cos{\\left(x \\right)} - 2 e^{x} \\sin{\\left(x \\right)} + 2 e^{x} \\cos{\\left(x \\right)} + 6 \\sin^{2}{\\left(x \\right)} + 6 \\cos^{2}{\\left(x \\right)}}{\\left(e^{x} + 3 \\cos{\\left(x \\right)}\\right)^{2}}\\\\ &=\\frac{- x^{2} e^{x} + 3 x^{2} \\sin{\\left(x \\right)} + 2 x e^{x} + 6 x \\cos{\\left(x \\right)} - 2 e^{x} \\sin{\\left(x \\right)} + 2 e^{x} \\cos{\\left(x \\right)} + 6 \\sin^{2}{\\left(x \\right)} + 6 \\cos^{2}{\\left(x \\right)}}{\\left(e^{x} + 3 \\cos{\\left(x \\right)}\\right)^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
